# My everyday loaf based on morph

starter:
  ap_flour
  water
  hydration = 100%

leaven:
  starter
  bread_flour = 5 * starter
  cold_water
  extra = -20g
  hydration = 100%

grain:
  prairie_gold
  hard_red
  spelt = 5%
  rye = 10%

dry:
  grain
  vwg = 3%
  potato_flakes = 5%
  flaxseed_meal = 5%
  yeast = 0.5%
  salt = 1.8%

wet:
  cold_water
  old_dough = 100g
  ascorbic_acid_1p = 50ppm * 100 * grain
  leaven = 40%
  olive_oil = 5%
  honey = 5%
  yogurt = 5%

dough:
  wet
  dry
  hydration = 70%
  old_dough = 0 - wet.old_dough # forgot to remove it
  total_flour = 500g # 9 inch

/*
August 28, 2026

Changes
* use rye instead of barley and buckwheat

Next time
* Knead less to avoid keyhole

Starter is 8 days old.

Mixed the leaven about 20:00 and onto the counter at 78F.

Started on dough at 8:00.

Leaven pH = 3.65 at 8:30 DT is 78F. It rose to the top of the 500ml
container and had started to fall.

Dry T=84. Wet T=61. 

Used the KA for mixing. Mixed about 8:40. Stopped after 3 minutes;
it was well mixed. DT after mixing is 71F. RT is 78F. 

30 minute rest in fridge.

Kneaded 10 minutes in KA. It was cleaning the bowl and looking great.

Into the cambro and into the fridge for 30 minutes.

S&F at 10:00. DT = 72F. Left on counter.

Into the pan at 11:00. Left on the counter at 78F.

Baked at 12:30.

I added 120ml of water to the pan before preheating the oven.


*/

